1
00:00:00,512 --> 00:00:02,931
[humming happily]

2
00:00:03,015 --> 00:00:04,349
[Anzu] It's finally here.

3
00:00:04,433 --> 00:00:05,934
Ishiai Koji's cat book!

4
00:00:06,017 --> 00:00:08,520
I love that Mom sends
pictures of Momohiki,

5
00:00:08,603 --> 00:00:10,772
but this is an extra cat boost for my day.

6
00:00:10,856 --> 00:00:13,316
Let the healing begin!
[smooches]

7
00:00:14,025 --> 00:00:17,446
[Anzu] Huh? Has it already been a month
since Kazuki moved in?

8
00:00:18,029 --> 00:00:20,782
Guess he'll be finding a new place soon.

9
00:00:21,533 --> 00:00:24,870
Living with Junta and Kazuki
has been surprisingly fun.

10
00:00:24,953 --> 00:00:27,164
It'll be strange when he moves out.

11
00:00:27,706 --> 00:00:28,749
ARISA: CAN WE MEET?

12
00:00:28,832 --> 00:00:31,293
[Anzu] Speaking of strange, I wonder
who that text was from--

13
00:00:31,376 --> 00:00:32,836
-[man] I know, right?
-[grunts]

14
00:00:32,919 --> 00:00:33,962
-[can clanks]
-[man grunts]

15
00:00:34,046 --> 00:00:35,088
[Anzu] My book!

16
00:00:36,298 --> 00:00:37,215
[sighs in relief]

17
00:00:38,300 --> 00:00:40,093
What the hell do you think you're doing?

18
00:00:40,177 --> 00:00:42,679
I was just waiting
for the light to change.

19
00:00:43,263 --> 00:00:46,099
[Anzu] He bumped into me.
I should be the one yelling.

20
00:00:46,183 --> 00:00:48,977
It's all thanks to you
that I dropped my coffee.

21
00:00:49,061 --> 00:00:50,812
-And ruined my shoes.
-[gasps]

22
00:00:50,896 --> 00:00:52,814
-[man] You're gonna pay for that!
-[Anzu] Hey!

23
00:00:53,648 --> 00:00:54,941
-Uh…
-That's enough.

24
00:00:56,234 --> 00:00:57,069
[Anzu] Huh?

25
00:00:58,153 --> 00:01:00,072
You're the one who bumped into her.

26
00:01:00,155 --> 00:01:02,282
[gasping]

27
00:01:02,365 --> 00:01:05,285
Ah, dude. You're, like, crazy hot.

28
00:01:05,368 --> 00:01:08,789
What do you say, you pay back
your little friend's debt with a date?

29
00:01:08,872 --> 00:01:10,207
[man laughing mischievously]

30
00:01:11,249 --> 00:01:13,376
[grunts in pain]

31
00:01:13,460 --> 00:01:15,629
-Don't ever touch me.
-[man] Ow…

32
00:01:15,712 --> 00:01:17,297
Now apologize to her.

33
00:01:17,881 --> 00:01:19,800
It's just a stupid book!

34
00:01:19,883 --> 00:01:21,760
[grunts]
Just a book?

35
00:01:22,385 --> 00:01:25,514
[Anzu] You have no idea what I've lost!

36
00:01:25,597 --> 00:01:27,808
[shouting] This book is worth
hours of healing!

37
00:01:28,975 --> 00:01:31,978
I curse you!
May stray cats infest your house

38
00:01:32,062 --> 00:01:33,897
and soak your bed in cat pee!

39
00:01:33,980 --> 00:01:36,149
You're gonna drill straight into my brain!

40
00:01:36,233 --> 00:01:37,901
-[growling]
-[screams]

41
00:01:37,984 --> 00:01:39,528
I'm sorry!

42
00:01:40,195 --> 00:01:41,905
-[man] Ow!
-Uh…

43
00:01:41,988 --> 00:01:45,200
[man] My head… the pain.
That chick's crazy.

44
00:01:45,283 --> 00:01:46,368
-[snorts]
-[startled gasps]

45
00:01:47,744 --> 00:01:50,914
Maybe next time
you'll be a little bit more respectful.

46
00:01:51,957 --> 00:01:53,875
[all gasp]

47
00:01:54,668 --> 00:01:56,503
-Let's go.
-[Anzu blows raspberry]

48
00:01:56,586 --> 00:01:59,131
-Your book okay? Sorry about those jerks.
-[gasps]

49
00:01:59,214 --> 00:02:00,966
Heh?
[sighs in relief]

50
00:02:01,466 --> 00:02:02,801
[Anzu exclaims]

51
00:02:04,052 --> 00:02:07,222
Oh yeah, the book's fine.
Thanks for saving me.

52
00:02:07,305 --> 00:02:09,015
Oh my gosh, she'll think I'm in love!

53
00:02:09,099 --> 00:02:11,977
I hope I don't look as dumb
as I feel right now!

54
00:02:12,978 --> 00:02:14,437
Did you really

55
00:02:14,521 --> 00:02:16,731
curse him with a cat-pee-soaked mattress?

56
00:02:16,815 --> 00:02:19,985
[Anzu] It was all I could think of.
You can never get that smell out.

57
00:02:20,068 --> 00:02:21,194
-[Tsukasa] Arisa.
-[both] Huh?

58
00:02:22,028 --> 00:02:23,071
Hey, Tsukasa.

59
00:02:23,155 --> 00:02:24,322
Kazuki?

60
00:02:24,406 --> 00:02:26,491
Hoshino? You know each other?

61
00:02:26,575 --> 00:02:27,784
Hoshino, like…

62
00:02:28,451 --> 00:02:30,620
Wait, are you Anzu Hoshino?

63
00:02:30,704 --> 00:02:31,788
Me? Um…

64
00:02:32,747 --> 00:02:34,791
I'm Arisa, Tsukasa's big sister.

65
00:02:34,875 --> 00:02:36,501
Thanks for looking after him.

66
00:02:36,585 --> 00:02:37,794
[chuckles]

67
00:02:38,879 --> 00:02:42,007
Uh, legendary good looks
run in your family.

68
00:02:42,090 --> 00:02:44,551
So bright, can't look directly at it!

69
00:02:44,634 --> 00:02:45,635
[Tsukasa] You're an idiot.

70
00:02:50,849 --> 00:02:52,851
[theme music]

71
00:04:16,101 --> 00:04:17,018
[birds chirping]

72
00:04:17,102 --> 00:04:19,145
#8 THE PHOENIX RISES! I AM A BIRD!

73
00:04:19,229 --> 00:04:23,066
Thanks for having me. Are you sure
that I'm not barging in here?

74
00:04:23,149 --> 00:04:24,234
Of course not.

75
00:04:24,776 --> 00:04:27,279
Thanks again
for letting Tsukasa stay here.

76
00:04:27,362 --> 00:04:29,197
A month is a long time.

77
00:04:29,948 --> 00:04:30,865
No, not at all.

78
00:04:30,949 --> 00:04:33,785
Really, it's been awesome
having him around.

79
00:04:33,868 --> 00:04:36,538
[Anzu] Not to mention
this whole thing is my fault.

80
00:04:37,706 --> 00:04:40,875
My mother and I
should have introduced ourselves sooner.

81
00:04:41,376 --> 00:04:43,336
-To be honest, we were a bit surprised.
-[grumbles]

82
00:04:43,420 --> 00:04:45,463
We didn't think he'd be staying this long.

83
00:04:45,547 --> 00:04:48,925
Between the pipe bursting
and the new phone, it's been chaotic.

84
00:04:49,009 --> 00:04:51,261
So I figured it was probably
best for me to come out

85
00:04:51,344 --> 00:04:52,929
and get the details in person.

86
00:04:53,555 --> 00:04:55,640
Oh yeah, that makes sense.

87
00:04:56,141 --> 00:04:59,561
[Anzu] The phone…
Yeah, that was my fault too.

88
00:04:59,644 --> 00:05:03,148
Oh. Hey, would you like
something to drink?

89
00:05:03,231 --> 00:05:06,192
I think we have some iced tea, or, um…

90
00:05:06,276 --> 00:05:08,778
-[Tsukasa] Uh, there's a fresh pitcher.
-Oh, that would be great.

91
00:05:08,862 --> 00:05:09,821
[chuckles]

92
00:05:10,905 --> 00:05:13,908
[Arisa clears throat]
Better let Mom know everything's okay.

93
00:05:15,410 --> 00:05:18,330
[Tsukasa] So, did something happen
at the station? You looked frazzled.

94
00:05:18,413 --> 00:05:23,293
Oh. This guy bumped into me,
then tried to pick a fight with me.

95
00:05:23,376 --> 00:05:24,210
[Tsukasa] What?

96
00:05:25,295 --> 00:05:27,922
But your sister totally saved me.

97
00:05:28,798 --> 00:05:30,633
Those guys didn't stand a chance.

98
00:05:30,717 --> 00:05:32,886
You know what? Your sister's really cool.

99
00:05:32,969 --> 00:05:35,055
Yeah, but she had a tendency
to find trouble.

100
00:05:36,556 --> 00:05:37,515
I'm sorry that happened.

101
00:05:38,016 --> 00:05:39,142
Nah, it's fine,

102
00:05:39,225 --> 00:05:42,937
'cause I cursed him with a mattress
completely soaked in cat pee!

103
00:05:43,021 --> 00:05:46,566
-So yeah, it's all good.
-[muffled laugh]

104
00:05:46,649 --> 00:05:50,987
[Tsukasa] Seriously?
A mattress soaked in cat pee?

105
00:05:51,071 --> 00:05:53,198
No, it really is the worst!

106
00:05:53,990 --> 00:05:54,991
[chuckles]

107
00:05:57,368 --> 00:05:58,703
[Anzu] Sorry to keep you waiting.

108
00:05:58,787 --> 00:06:00,538
All good, thanks.

109
00:06:01,998 --> 00:06:05,085
Kazuki, I'm just curious.

110
00:06:05,168 --> 00:06:07,295
Why did you wanna go to our school
and live alone?

111
00:06:07,796 --> 00:06:08,797
[both gasp]

112
00:06:08,880 --> 00:06:09,714
[both sigh]

113
00:06:09,798 --> 00:06:12,509
[Anzu] Uh, you don't have to answer that.
I shouldn't have asked.

114
00:06:12,592 --> 00:06:15,970
-[whimpers]
-Hmm… Well, how do I say this?

115
00:06:19,808 --> 00:06:21,976
-Huh?
-[soft chuckle]

116
00:06:22,560 --> 00:06:24,687
Our father's a real piece of garbage.

117
00:06:24,771 --> 00:06:25,605
SHIT

118
00:06:25,688 --> 00:06:27,482
Piece of garbage?

119
00:06:28,066 --> 00:06:30,151
Yup. That's why our mom decided

120
00:06:30,235 --> 00:06:32,320
it was best for Tsukasa
to go to school out here.

121
00:06:32,403 --> 00:06:33,238
Oh.

122
00:06:34,614 --> 00:06:36,407
I'm not wrong, am I?

123
00:06:36,491 --> 00:06:37,492
No.

124
00:06:39,953 --> 00:06:42,747
I was really worried
when I heard you'd be living alone.

125
00:06:43,581 --> 00:06:46,668
I'm relieved you're staying
with someone sweet like Anzu.

126
00:06:46,751 --> 00:06:48,670
[phone vibrates]

127
00:06:50,213 --> 00:06:51,256
Oh, Makoto.

128
00:06:52,674 --> 00:06:54,384
Um, hey.

129
00:06:54,467 --> 00:06:55,385
What's up?

130
00:06:57,762 --> 00:07:00,598
-[Arisa] Who's Makoto?
-[Anzu] He's a friend from school.

131
00:07:01,266 --> 00:07:02,267
Oh.

132
00:07:02,767 --> 00:07:05,270
Hey, what's Tsukasa like
at school, anyway?

133
00:07:05,770 --> 00:07:09,649
Well, uh, he's popular
but keeps to himself.

134
00:07:11,109 --> 00:07:13,570
Being reserved makes everyone
like him even more.

135
00:07:13,653 --> 00:07:14,821
And you?

136
00:07:15,447 --> 00:07:17,740
-You seem to like him too, huh?
-[chokes]

137
00:07:17,824 --> 00:07:19,075
[spits, gags]

138
00:07:19,659 --> 00:07:20,493
Huh?

139
00:07:20,577 --> 00:07:21,494
[in deep voice]
It's not like that.

140
00:07:21,578 --> 00:07:23,663
I swear on my unborn descendants.

141
00:07:23,746 --> 00:07:24,873
[Arisa] That's a bit extreme.

142
00:07:25,415 --> 00:07:28,585
In fact, I didn't like him
when I first met him.

143
00:07:29,919 --> 00:07:31,087
But…

144
00:07:31,171 --> 00:07:33,381
I'm glad I took the time
to get to know him better.

145
00:07:34,090 --> 00:07:36,676
'Cause, you know,
now he's a really great friend.

146
00:07:37,760 --> 00:07:39,179
[Arisa chuckles softly]

147
00:07:39,929 --> 00:07:43,224
You know, he used to be
a really social kid.

148
00:07:43,308 --> 00:07:46,186
He was always smiling,
befriending everyone he met.

149
00:07:47,020 --> 00:07:48,688
I can't picture that.

150
00:07:48,771 --> 00:07:50,273
[Arisa chuckles]
I know, right?

151
00:07:51,274 --> 00:07:54,569
There was a problem
back when he was in junior high.

152
00:07:54,652 --> 00:07:57,322
Ever since then, he sort of shut down.

153
00:07:57,405 --> 00:08:01,493
So before, the way he was laughing
with you, I haven't seen that side

154
00:08:01,576 --> 00:08:04,329
of my little brother
in a really long time.

155
00:08:04,996 --> 00:08:05,872
Huh?

156
00:08:06,414 --> 00:08:08,500
You bring it out of him, Anzu.

157
00:08:09,083 --> 00:08:10,627
Really, it's not--

158
00:08:10,710 --> 00:08:11,836
-[door shuts]
-[both] Huh?

159
00:08:11,920 --> 00:08:13,838
He wanted me to go to a movie,

160
00:08:14,380 --> 00:08:16,841
but I think he really just wanted
someone to vent to.

161
00:08:17,717 --> 00:08:19,636
-[Anzu] About what?
-Oh…

162
00:08:20,345 --> 00:08:22,388
Something about his sister
stealing his last pudding.

163
00:08:22,472 --> 00:08:23,348
MAKOTO
IT WAS DELICIOUS

164
00:08:24,349 --> 00:08:25,475
[chuckles]
Tell him next time

165
00:08:25,558 --> 00:08:27,018
to write his name on it.

166
00:08:27,101 --> 00:08:28,603
[Tsukasa] He did. She ate it anyway.

167
00:08:29,312 --> 00:08:33,149
Hmm. There's no stronger grudge
than one held over food.

168
00:08:33,233 --> 00:08:34,484
Is it that big a deal?

169
00:08:35,068 --> 00:08:36,694
I don't make the rules.

170
00:08:37,570 --> 00:08:39,572
[light music]

171
00:08:44,577 --> 00:08:46,079
About your friend, Anzu.

172
00:08:47,080 --> 00:08:49,374
She's sweet. I'm just surprised
you're friends with her.

173
00:08:49,457 --> 00:08:50,291
[chuckles]

174
00:08:50,375 --> 00:08:53,002
I thought
you were still avoiding all girls.

175
00:08:55,171 --> 00:08:56,714
[sighs]

176
00:08:56,798 --> 00:08:59,592
Yeah, I know. I wasn't planning on it.

177
00:09:00,593 --> 00:09:03,763
But she's different.
I feel more at ease with her.

178
00:09:04,430 --> 00:09:07,350
Tsukasa, why don't you just
stay here a while?

179
00:09:07,850 --> 00:09:09,060
Huh?

180
00:09:09,143 --> 00:09:10,562
Calm down, it's a joke.

181
00:09:11,271 --> 00:09:13,022
-[sighs in relief]
-Uh… uh…

182
00:09:14,190 --> 00:09:15,775
Uh, well…

183
00:09:16,317 --> 00:09:18,736
[Anzu] I don't mind if you don't mind.

184
00:09:18,820 --> 00:09:19,946
Hm?

185
00:09:21,155 --> 00:09:23,116
You've been so helpful around here.

186
00:09:23,199 --> 00:09:25,868
And maybe it's just me,
but I think it's been a lot of fun

187
00:09:25,952 --> 00:09:26,995
living with you and Junta.

188
00:09:27,745 --> 00:09:30,999
[Anzu] Not to mention Riri's scheming
if you leave Junta and I alone.

189
00:09:31,082 --> 00:09:32,292
Most importantly,

190
00:09:32,375 --> 00:09:35,670
you're the only one brave enough
to kill all those bugs!

191
00:09:35,753 --> 00:09:37,005
-[groans]
-[Tsukasa chuckles]

192
00:09:37,088 --> 00:09:39,048
If it's that important to you,

193
00:09:39,841 --> 00:09:41,301
then I guess I'll stay.

194
00:09:43,595 --> 00:09:44,596
Hm.

195
00:09:45,346 --> 00:09:48,516
[sighs in relief]
Yeah? This will be great!

196
00:09:48,600 --> 00:09:50,351
There's another show
I've been dying to watch.

197
00:09:50,435 --> 00:09:51,269
Sure.

198
00:09:51,936 --> 00:09:55,481
I get it now. That's why
you never wanted to talk about her.

199
00:09:56,858 --> 00:09:59,235
You were embarrassed I'd figure it out.

200
00:09:59,319 --> 00:10:00,778
That she makes you smile again.

201
00:10:02,280 --> 00:10:03,156
Um…

202
00:10:05,074 --> 00:10:07,160
-Wait, do you like--
-It's not like that.

203
00:10:08,286 --> 00:10:10,246
With Hoshino, I can be myself.

204
00:10:10,747 --> 00:10:13,082
For me, that's all I need.

205
00:10:14,292 --> 00:10:15,418
[Tsukasa sighs]

206
00:10:18,004 --> 00:10:19,005
[Arisa] Okay.

207
00:10:19,964 --> 00:10:21,966
[soft music]

208
00:10:22,467 --> 00:10:24,385
[water running]

209
00:10:25,178 --> 00:10:27,555
[Anzu] I'm glad
I met Kazuki's sister today.

210
00:10:27,639 --> 00:10:29,932
I learned a lot more about him.

211
00:10:30,725 --> 00:10:31,893
[door opens]

212
00:10:31,976 --> 00:10:33,311
Hey, you're back.

213
00:10:34,854 --> 00:10:37,106
You have the coolest sister.

214
00:10:37,190 --> 00:10:39,651
I loved getting to meet her.
[gasps]

215
00:10:39,734 --> 00:10:42,362
I should have worn something nicer.
This outfit sucks.

216
00:10:44,238 --> 00:10:46,908
I really assumed you thought
that outfit was appropriate

217
00:10:46,991 --> 00:10:47,909
to meet guests.

218
00:10:47,992 --> 00:10:49,243
No way.

219
00:10:49,327 --> 00:10:51,663
I learned a lot
when we went shopping together.

220
00:10:51,746 --> 00:10:54,415
I've tried to be more mindful
about what I wear since then.

221
00:10:55,625 --> 00:10:58,378
[Anzu] Man, I wish I had
a big sister like her.

222
00:11:00,046 --> 00:11:00,963
Hoshino.

223
00:11:01,464 --> 00:11:03,758
What Arisa said
about why I lived by myself…

224
00:11:05,843 --> 00:11:06,761
Yeah?

225
00:11:07,428 --> 00:11:08,471
Uh, uh--

226
00:11:09,305 --> 00:11:10,264
[exhales deeply]

227
00:11:10,890 --> 00:11:13,476
Never mind. Maybe another day.

228
00:11:15,186 --> 00:11:16,354
Hmm…

229
00:11:17,230 --> 00:11:19,190
[Anzu] Uh, okay.

230
00:11:22,693 --> 00:11:24,445
[Anzu] Is it just me or…

231
00:11:25,530 --> 00:11:27,532
-[Riri] Is this warm feeling friendship?
-[grunts]

232
00:11:27,615 --> 00:11:30,618
Or is this excitement? Love!

233
00:11:31,202 --> 00:11:34,372
Yay! Great job, Anzu, I'm so proud of you!

234
00:11:34,455 --> 00:11:36,749
You were able to get
his big sister's approval,

235
00:11:36,833 --> 00:11:38,418
even just like that.

236
00:11:38,501 --> 00:11:40,753
I tell you how can you find love,
it's so fulfilling.

237
00:11:40,837 --> 00:11:45,633
-Now, let's keep this up--
-You know what? I didn't miss you one bit!

238
00:11:45,716 --> 00:11:47,343
[Anzu roars]

239
00:11:47,427 --> 00:11:50,138
-[slaps]
-Come on!

240
00:11:50,221 --> 00:11:51,722
A FEW DAYS LATER

241
00:11:52,598 --> 00:11:55,393
In order to address low birth rate issues,

242
00:11:57,145 --> 00:12:01,399
Anzu was gifted a real-life dating sim
called Romantic Thriller.

243
00:12:01,482 --> 00:12:03,901
And after many perfect scenarios,

244
00:12:03,985 --> 00:12:08,573
I am reporting that there has been
zero romantic development.

245
00:12:08,656 --> 00:12:10,908
I can't turn this in!

246
00:12:10,992 --> 00:12:12,994
[frustrated groan]

247
00:12:14,495 --> 00:12:17,415
Clearly, I have a lot more research to do.

248
00:12:18,040 --> 00:12:19,876
I have an excellent idea!

249
00:12:19,959 --> 00:12:21,919
-We can go on a date.
-What?

250
00:12:22,670 --> 00:12:25,590
[Riri] I need to experience
what a real-life date is like,

251
00:12:25,673 --> 00:12:27,425
so you and I will go on a mock date.

252
00:12:27,508 --> 00:12:28,926
A mock date?

253
00:12:29,010 --> 00:12:31,262
What are you even talking about?

254
00:12:32,013 --> 00:12:34,015
I'm so over your nonsense.

255
00:12:34,515 --> 00:12:37,894
[chuckling]
Aw, don't be such a meanie!

256
00:12:37,977 --> 00:12:38,936
-Ha!
-[explosion]

257
00:12:39,020 --> 00:12:42,440
-[Anzu] Huh?
-What if I look like this instead?

258
00:12:42,523 --> 00:12:43,357
[chuckles]

259
00:12:43,441 --> 00:12:45,443
[Anzu] Wait!
There's a boy version of you too?

260
00:12:46,027 --> 00:12:46,986
[groans]

261
00:12:47,069 --> 00:12:49,697
Whatever. Doesn't change anything.

262
00:12:50,281 --> 00:12:52,200
I'm not asking you to do this for free.

263
00:12:52,283 --> 00:12:54,202
-[Anzu] Huh?
-[Rio] I'll buy you those cat pajamas

264
00:12:54,285 --> 00:12:56,787
you saw in the mall.
The one with the hoodies and tail.

265
00:12:58,122 --> 00:12:59,248
[in deep voice]
It's a deal.

266
00:12:59,332 --> 00:13:00,791
[groans in pain]
Let go!

267
00:13:01,542 --> 00:13:04,879
Whoo! Can't believe I'm on my first date!

268
00:13:04,962 --> 00:13:06,172
Tell me…

269
00:13:06,255 --> 00:13:08,257
[bright music]

270
00:13:08,841 --> 00:13:10,676
Why did I have to dress up for this?

271
00:13:10,760 --> 00:13:12,303
It's a date.

272
00:13:12,386 --> 00:13:14,555
We're not hanging out
at a rest stop for truckers.

273
00:13:14,639 --> 00:13:16,891
Hey! Do I really dress that badly?

274
00:13:16,974 --> 00:13:18,434
Yep, just the worst.

275
00:13:19,268 --> 00:13:20,937
Now, on with our date!

276
00:13:21,020 --> 00:13:21,938
Ugh!

277
00:13:22,522 --> 00:13:25,608
-[whimpers]
-Easy there, I'm not some sort of pervert.

278
00:13:26,359 --> 00:13:28,444
Holding hands is what you do on dates.

279
00:13:28,528 --> 00:13:31,280
I don't care. I don't want people
getting the wrong idea about us.

280
00:13:31,781 --> 00:13:33,950
-[grunts]
-Hmm…

281
00:13:34,534 --> 00:13:36,494
[Rio] I'll buy you another cat shirt!

282
00:13:37,620 --> 00:13:39,080
[Anzu grunts]

283
00:13:39,664 --> 00:13:41,457
-Fine, then hold my hand.
-Ow, ow, ouch!

284
00:13:42,250 --> 00:13:43,543
So, where are we going?

285
00:13:45,169 --> 00:13:47,630
The most classic of dating activities.
The movies.

286
00:13:48,422 --> 00:13:49,298
[laughter]

287
00:13:49,382 --> 00:13:53,678
[Rio] A romantic movie always
gets the couple in the mood for love.

288
00:13:53,761 --> 00:13:55,680
Slowly their hands touch.

289
00:13:56,264 --> 00:13:57,265
-[girl gasps]
-Huh?

290
00:13:58,266 --> 00:14:00,685
[Rio] And then, their lips touch.

291
00:14:01,269 --> 00:14:02,395
[smooching]

292
00:14:02,478 --> 00:14:03,479
You're twisted.

293
00:14:04,272 --> 00:14:06,190
[indistinct chatter]

294
00:14:08,776 --> 00:14:10,861
Is there anything good out right now?

295
00:14:11,445 --> 00:14:13,531
Oh, any cat movies?

296
00:14:13,614 --> 00:14:15,074
[Rio] No cats! We're on a date,

297
00:14:15,157 --> 00:14:16,534
so we're definitely watching
a romantic movie!

298
00:14:16,617 --> 00:14:17,869
ETERNAL STAR

299
00:14:18,452 --> 00:14:21,247
What? That looks so lame.

300
00:14:21,330 --> 00:14:24,208
One of those tearjerkers
where the girl dies in the end.

301
00:14:24,292 --> 00:14:25,626
Tearjerkers are great!

302
00:14:25,710 --> 00:14:28,963
So much romance,
it'll be the perfect reference material!

303
00:14:29,463 --> 00:14:31,883
Using this kind of movie
is a reference…

304
00:14:32,633 --> 00:14:34,051
doesn't bode well for me.

305
00:14:35,928 --> 00:14:36,888
[Makoto groans]

306
00:14:37,471 --> 00:14:38,764
That was so good!

307
00:14:39,348 --> 00:14:40,892
We've got to do this more often.

308
00:14:40,975 --> 00:14:42,894
-[Tsukasa] Yeah.
-[Makoto] Hey, look!

309
00:14:42,977 --> 00:14:44,729
-Need the bathroom first.
-[Makoto] Hosshi!

310
00:14:44,812 --> 00:14:46,230
-[both] Huh?
-[Makoto] Hey, you!

311
00:14:46,314 --> 00:14:48,399
-[Anzu gasps]
-Looking good all dressed up.

312
00:14:48,983 --> 00:14:50,651
Kazuki, Makoto.

313
00:14:51,777 --> 00:14:52,737
-Huh?
-Uh?

314
00:14:52,820 --> 00:14:53,905
[gasps]

315
00:14:53,988 --> 00:14:55,907
-[Anzu] Oh crap!
-[Anzu grunting]

316
00:14:55,990 --> 00:14:57,283
How's it going?

317
00:14:57,366 --> 00:15:00,328
I'm Anzu's cousin, Rio. Rio Fushigi.

318
00:15:00,411 --> 00:15:01,871
I'm Riri's twin brother.

319
00:15:01,954 --> 00:15:03,664
[Anzu] Yeah, nice backstory.

320
00:15:03,748 --> 00:15:05,833
This is just great.
All the people in this town

321
00:15:05,917 --> 00:15:07,668
and we had to run into these two?

322
00:15:07,752 --> 00:15:09,503
Wait, didn't he set this up?

323
00:15:09,587 --> 00:15:12,256
All right, we better get going then.
We're on a date.

324
00:15:12,340 --> 00:15:14,175
-[smacks]
-Hey, don't say stuff like that.

325
00:15:14,258 --> 00:15:17,094
Ignore him.
Rio just likes to mess around sometimes.

326
00:15:17,178 --> 00:15:18,012
Bye!

327
00:15:18,512 --> 00:15:21,432
-See ya, Hosshi. Oh, and Hosshi's cousin.
-[growls]

328
00:15:22,016 --> 00:15:24,936
They seem oddly close
for being cousins, don't you think?

329
00:15:25,978 --> 00:15:26,812
[Anzu grunts]

330
00:15:28,898 --> 00:15:30,149
What's your problem?

331
00:15:30,232 --> 00:15:31,984
Calm down, it's a mock date.

332
00:15:32,068 --> 00:15:33,653
Gotta treat it like the real thing.

333
00:15:33,736 --> 00:15:35,863
You're gonna give them
the wrong idea about me.

334
00:15:35,947 --> 00:15:38,032
I'll sue you for defamation!

335
00:15:38,115 --> 00:15:40,409
The lady doth protest too much.

336
00:15:40,993 --> 00:15:44,580
[Anzu] Strange. Usually, he'd get Kazuki
and the others involved

337
00:15:44,664 --> 00:15:46,916
in some crazy dating scenarios.

338
00:15:46,999 --> 00:15:50,086
Maybe he really is trying
to learn about dating.

339
00:15:50,169 --> 00:15:51,170
Too bad for him,

340
00:15:51,253 --> 00:15:54,423
whatever he learns here,
I'll just destroy it!

341
00:15:55,716 --> 00:15:57,385
-[chuckles mischievously]
-What's with that face?

342
00:15:57,468 --> 00:16:00,429
Smiling weird like that makes you look
like you're coming unhinged.

343
00:16:01,472 --> 00:16:03,432
There's nothing better than popcorn

